course: dictionary
lesson: 12081
title: Cloning: exact copies
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cloning means making an exact copy of something. The word appears in science, gardening, computing and safety lessons, so the words around it tell you which kind of copy is meant. «Scientists used cloning to make a copy of a sheep called Dolly.» The sentence says copy, so cloning means making a copy.
explain: «Gardeners use cloning to grow new plants from cuttings.» The clues are plants and cuttings: a new plant grows from a piece of an old one, and it is the same as the parent plant. Try the swap: "Gardeners use copying to grow new plants from cuttings" still makes sense, so cloning means copying.
explain: «Police warned us that card cloning can steal money.» Here cloning is secret and it is a crime, because someone copies bank card details to take money. The clues are police, warned and steal. Cloning can be useful or harmful, so always read the words around it.
fact: Cloning means making an exact copy of something.
fact: In science, cloning means making a copy of a living thing with the same genes, from one of its cells.
fact: Identical twins are natural clones, because they share the same genes.
fact: In computing, cloning means copying something exactly, such as a hard drive or a website.
fact: Card cloning is a crime: it means copying someone's bank card details secretly to steal money.
exercise: «Scientists used cloning to make a copy of a sheep called Dolly.» What does cloning mean here? | Painting a picture of a sheep | *Making an exact copy of a living thing | Shearing wool from a sheep | Feeding animals on a farm
exercise: «Gardeners use cloning to grow new plants from cuttings.» What is the new plant grown from? | *A cutting from an old plant | A plastic pot | A bag of soil
exercise: «Police warned us that card cloning can steal money.» Is card cloning good or bad? | Good, because it helps you shop | Good, because it makes exact copies of games | Neither good nor bad, it is only a game | *Bad, because it is a crime
test: In computing, what does cloning mean? | *Copying something exactly, such as a hard drive | Deleting old files to save space | Painting a picture of a computer | Typing very fast
test: Why are identical twins called natural clones? | *They have the same genes | They always wear matching clothes | They live in the same house | They are the same height
exam: Which word means making an exact copy of a living thing from one of its cells? | Cooking | Cutting | Crawling | *Cloning
